{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/29888-how-to-detect-and-deal-with-urged-and-claimed","id":29888,"title":"How to detect and deal with Urged and Claimed?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-14T07:12:15-08:00","id":29888,"title":"How to detect and deal with Urged and Claimed?","content":"Greetings!<br /> <br /> I have some trouble in understanding how the Uratha can actually know if someone is urged or claimed. Can they sense it somehow? Are there special powers i oversaw? And how can someone who is urged be saved from the spirits posession? Hope you guys can enlighten me on that subject.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1671-mythforger","name":"Mythforger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1671_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T07:58:14-08:00","id":29908,"title":"","content":"For urged, they get rolls to detect spirits in twilight. Wits+Occult+Primal Urge.<br /> <br /> For claimed? they mutate. These changes usually come with disfigurements and odd scents coming from a person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T08:31:22-08:00","id":29927,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the answer. But isnt the spirit hidden inside the human if it is urging him? Can they just roll for every guy in the room and just know somehow he is urged? And is there a method to &quot;save&quot; a claimed one? Or is the specific human forever lost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1671,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1671-mythforger","user":"Mythforger","date":". 12-14-2013, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1671-mythforger","name":"Mythforger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1671_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T13:38:24-08:00","id":31179,"title":"","content":"Well, not being able to detect them easily is part of their schtick. It's one of the reasons they're scary, because they can't bee spotted simply with the right chant or fetish (though, I suppose, one could always try to build a fetish just for that).<br /> <br /> For the greatest amount of information, which will answer all your questions, see the chapter devoted to them in <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/2402/Predators?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Predators</a>.<br /> <br /> Short answers to the ones I know for certain:<br /> Yes, there are methods for saving the mount.<br /> Yes, the specific human can be lost for ever, details are in the above mentioned book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T17:25:03-08:00","id":31347,"title":"","content":"As I am currently running a Forsaken game and have had to decide answers for some of these in session, here is the way I run it.<br /> <br /> When a spirit Urges a person, they're just using the Fetter numen/manifestation, which requires they remain within five yards of their fetter - although they remain in a state of Twilight, and so can occupy the same physical space, literally hiding inside of them. When the spirit is lackadaisical, it could be seen hanging out around its fetter; when its actively hiding from scrutiny, I give it a concealment bonus to its stealth roll, based on the difference in size. Abstract spirits tend to be size 3 or thereabouts, so I give a -2 penalty when they hide inside of a human; oddly shaped or larger spirits give a bonus.<br /> When it comes to detection, I allow their gaze into Twilight to apply for the whole room, not scrutinizing an individual. I also give passive rolls for sensing a spirit in Twilight, especially if its doing things (usually a harder dice pool, like just Wits, and with hints rather than full descriptions; the abilities which allow detecting spirits are supposed to be activated, after all).<br /> <br /> Using the description from Geist, and actual possession looks like a strange double image or negative photo effect when looking into Twilight, as the spirit and human take up the same space, but imperfectly so.<br /> Claimed, however, don't have anything in Twilight which cues them off; rather its a matter of bizarre mutations and scents, or by the behavior of the character. Claimed can be very subtle when they set out to be (especially with the 'masked power' aspect); they should be serious, challenging antagonists.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for saving humans that are Claimed, the spirit is able to untangle itself and leave, and it can do so delicately to leave the human soul intact. It's a difficult process (described in <i>Predators</i>), and its in the hands of the Claiming spirit. It's not a great solution, but claiming is a pretty powerful thing. I'd allow for research into particular rituals or fetishes, or spirits which can assist/force the untangling, but it should be a unique and difficult task every time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T01:38:46-08:00","id":31548,"title":"","content":"Very good ideas Seraph. I will absolutely use that. Thank you!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1671-mythforger","name":"Mythforger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1671_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T16:46:57-08:00","id":31995,"title":"","content":"I'm glad that I could help!<br /> <br /> [Addendum:] Regarding ending possession, geist also says that if you can interact with Twilight beings, you can literally grapple the possessing entity and pull them out of the person, ending their control. I don't think werewolves have any powers which let them shift into Twilight and do that, but their totem might be able to.<br /> There are some &quot;maybe&quot; abilities, though. For example, there is a rite which allows natural weapons to attack spirits in Twilight; it doesn't shift claws into Twilight, so I'd rule that it still hurts the host, but maybe not as much.<br /> According to GMC, a werewolves with an honorary rank of 2 or more higher than a spirit, their attacks count as a bane - which deals Lethal if they're in Twilight; again, I'd still have that hurt the host, but it might be useful.<br /> GMC also states that using bans, banes, abjuration, or exorcism will end a possession as well.<br /> <br /> These could work for spirits just Urging as well. For Claimed, however, they still suffer from bans and banes, but they can't be exorcised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 12-17-2013, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T02:42:29-08:00","id":32246,"title":"","content":"Kitty: Blessing of the Spirit Hunt, rank 2 rite, lets them touch spirits in Twilight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T03:08:55-08:00","id":32253,"title":"","content":"That was the rite I was referring to as a &quot;maybe&quot;. It specifically allows their fangs and claws to harm spirits in Twilight, however the rite doesn't make the werewolf any less physically tangible; hence my interpretation that any damage done to a spirit in a possession likewise harms the host. I don't know of an ability which lets them actually change their state of existence entirely into Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T03:20:27-08:00","id":32260,"title":"","content":"So the pack could try to lure the spirit out of hiding inside the Urged. And then get the creep and kick its butt with the help of Blessing of the Spirit Hunt? <br /> Maybe they could lure it out with its bane or something. Nice picture i get there. I know that there are later rituals for banishing an spirit back to where it belongs. <br /> But since my young pack is playing a loosely version of the Manitou Springs Demo, and there are Spirits urging everyone everywhere, they really need some ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1671-mythforger","name":"Mythforger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1671_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T01:19:25-08:00","id":35444,"title":"","content":"Still some confusion here.<br /> Ephsy: From where do you have the roll they get for spotting spirits in Twilight? I can not find anything about that. Blessing of the Spirit Hunt just allows them to hurt incorperal beeings. Not to lsee them into Twilight. There has to be something hidden in the core book that i miss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1671-mythforger","name":"Mythforger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1671_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T01:51:44-08:00","id":35459,"title":"","content":"Grappling is a form of attack.<br /> <br /> Dual Senses, pg 252, second paragraph.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T04:11:08-08:00","id":35496,"title":"","content":"Okay... How could i miss that?! BIG Thanks to you Ephsy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1671-mythforger","name":"Mythforger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1671_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T09:33:24-08:00","id":38311,"title":"","content":"For detecting the Claimed I usually let my players gets wind of some strange behavior in their territory, like huge amounts of glass being smashed, or series of incidents of people setting themselves on fire and things like that. Once they've got something to go on the players are usually fairly quick in seeing if there's supernatural or mundane causes and then acts accordingly.<br /> <br /> But takinga look in the shadows for how it looks around someone is usually a pretty good way to detect spirit activity. They also sometimes just kills people who they have strong reasons to think MAY be Ridden. Cruel, yes, but they've gotten a fair few this ways as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}